From 1cbe2ba15eae490238c9f047948d0105aad0552c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] opcodes: KNC instruction set tables

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: the 32 KNC mask instructions (VEX), jknzd/jkzd
in the escape-less VEX map (VexOpcode=VEX), and the KNC vector
instructions in the MVEX encoding (MVex; Intel called it EVEX before
AVX-512 existed), with their operand types (RegZMM, RegMask, Zmmword,
Imm2 for rounding/SAE, Vec_Disp8) and modifiers (swizzle, broadcast,
up/down conversion, EH, element size, compressed disp8 shift).
zmm16-31 carry RegVRex.  -march=k1om gets an explicit CPU flag set
instead of "unknown".

Intel's L1OM (Knights Ferry) vector ISA, the modifiers only it uses,
and vpackstore{h,l}pgps (VecType 5, which Intel's assembler aborts on)
are left out.

On 2.45 CpuK1OMNI makes the CPU flags six words; the flag helpers in gas
handle a sixth one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
